cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Efesto, please cite this software and the original sources
  relevant to the HMM profiles and external tools used in your analysis.
type: software
title: "Efesto: annotation of metal cycling, acquisition and resistance genes"
version: 1.0.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
authors:
  - given-names: Luigi
    family-names: Gallucci
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0892-6796"
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Molecular Ecology, Max Planck Institute for Marine
      Microbiology, Bremen, Germany
  - given-names: Anke
    family-names: Meyerdierks
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8834-5446"
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Molecular Ecology, Max Planck Institute for Marine
      Microbiology, Bremen, Germany
  - given-names: Rudolf
    family-names: Amann
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0846-7372"
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Molecular Ecology, Max Planck Institute for Marine
      Microbiology, Bremen, Germany
repository-code: "https://github.com/l-gallucci/Efesto"
url: "https://l-gallucci.github.io/Efesto/"
abstract: >-
  Efesto annotates metal cycling, acquisition and resistance genes in genomes
  and metagenomes using profile HMMs, gene neighbourhoods and optional evidence
  from operon prediction, orthology, topology and structural comparisons.
  All Efesto-owned code, standalone tooling, tests and project documentation
  are AGPLv3-licensed. HMMs and other third-party resources retain their source-specific terms;
  see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the per-model license/source table.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - metagenomics
  - metal cycling
  - iron cycling
  - hidden Markov models
  - functional annotation
